source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Two backslashes hide the closer with body text in front of them just as they do alone, so no span forms and the pair renders as a forced newline after the body; jiro refuses the span too and reads the same hard break between the literal braces.
-- input.jira --
{{a\\}}
-- rendered.html --
<p>{{a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />}}</p>
-- want.md --
{{a\
}}
